pulls.body:
This PR kills 3 mutants from https://mutanthub.space/mutants in validation.cpp 
I batched them together because the assertions are within the same test

Mutants killed:

Mutant 4388: validation.cpp ActivateBestChains, && → ||

```diff
@@ -6482,7 +6482,7 @@ util::Result<void> ChainstateManager::ActivateBestChains()
         for (const auto& chainstate : m_chainstates) {
-            if (chainstate && chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
+            if (chainstate || chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
                 chainstates.push_back(chainstate.get());
```

Mutant 4385: validation.cpp GetPruneRange, + 1 → - 1

```diff
@@ -6447,7 +6447,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
-        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight + 1;
+        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight - 1;
```

Mutant 4386: validation.cpp GetPruneRange, - → + MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP

```diff
@@ -6451,7 +6451,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
     int max_prune = std::max<int>(
-        0, m_chain.Height() - static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
+        0, m_chain.Height() + static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
```

The existing "Duplicate inputs" case only has two inputs, so the duplicate is always the last one. This PR adds a case with inputs A, A, B so that the duplicate-input check in `CheckTransaction` is exercised when the duplicate is not the last input.

It kills the following mutant (https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4676):

```diff
diff --git a/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp b/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
index 473538e4fe..3cbda6c0aa 100644
--- a/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
+++ b/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ bool CheckTransaction(const CTransaction& tx, TxValidationState& state)
     // the underlying coins database.
     std::set<COutPoint> vInOutPoints;
     for (const auto& txin : tx.vin) {
-        if (!vInOutPoints.insert(txin.prevout).second)
+        if (!vInOutPoints.insert(txin.prevout).second && &txin == &tx.vin.back())
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-inputs-duplicate");
     }
```

The existing max-conflict  cases fail on the parent alone, so the package-level limit check never runs. The new case uses a 0-fee parent so the package is evaluated as a whole. The parent hits the limit and the child's one extra conflict pushes it over.


It kills mutant https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4673 (fails in `test_package_rbf_max_conflicts`):

```diff
diff --git a/src/validation.cpp b/src/validation.cpp
index 57048ac374..2bb5188046 100644
--- a/src/validation.cpp
+++ b/src/validation.cpp
@@ -1067,7 +1067,7 @@ bool MemPoolAccept::PackageRBFChecks(const std::vector<CTransactionRef>& txns,
     // This limit is not increased in a package RBF. Use the aggregate number of transactions.
     CTxMemPool::setEntries all_conflicts;
     if (const auto err_string{GetEntriesForConflicts(*child_ws.m_ptx, m_pool, direct_conflict_iters,
-                                                     all_conflicts)}) {
+                                                     all_conflicts)}; false) {
         return package_state.Invalid(PackageValidationResult::PCKG_POLICY,
                                      "package RBF failed: too many potential replacements", *err_string);
     }
```
